    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="lede">
          Shaklee Life Shake is a solid plant-based meal shake with 20 g of soy or pea protein, 6 g of fiber and 0 g of sugar per serving, but at about $4.92 per 25 g of protein it costs two to five times as much as comparable Amazon powders. Membership narrows the gap. Below: the label, the testing claims, the real cost and cheaper swaps.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Shaklee Protein Powder: The Short Answer
          </h2>

          <p>
            Shaklee protein powder is a well-formulated but expensive vegan meal shake. Life Shake, the product most people mean by Shaklee protein, gives 20 g of soy or pea protein, 6 g of fiber, 0 g of sugar and 25 vitamins and minerals per two-scoop serving, per the label at the time of writing. It is not certified by NSF, Informed Sport or BSCG; Shaklee relies on its own testing. At $110.25 for 28 servings, it costs about $4.92 per 25 g of protein.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>Buy it if</strong> you are a Shaklee member paying the member price, you want a single scoop that replaces a light meal with vitamins and fiber built in, and you prefer soy or pea protein with no artificial sweeteners. <strong>Skip it if</strong> you mainly want protein per dollar, need a sport-certified product for drug-tested competition, or are watching sodium closely. A plain soy isolate or a Garden of Life meal shake covers the same ground for a fraction of the cost.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-4">Life Shake Soy by the Numbers</p>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 text-center">
              <div>
                <p class="text-3xl font-black text-white">20 g</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">Protein per 2 scoops</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="text-3xl font-black text-[#38BDF8]">110</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">Calories (French Vanilla)</p>
              </div>
