                <p class="text-3xl font-black text-white">0 g</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">Sugar, per the label</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="text-3xl font-black text-[#38BDF8]">$4.92</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">Per 25 g at retail</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Picks -->
        <div id="top-picks" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. Shaklee Protein Shakes and the Amazon Alternatives
          </h2>

          <p>
            Shaklee's Life Shake is sold through Shaklee's own site and its distributors, not on Amazon, so the first two cards have no Amazon link. Shaklee's whey does appear on Amazon. The last two cards are the closest Amazon alternatives we found, with the Amazon price we saw on November 20, 2026.
          </p>

          {PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => (
            <ProductCard product={product} rank={index + 1} />
          ))}
        </div>

        <div id="what-is-it" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            3. What Is Shaklee Protein Powder Made Of?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Shaklee protein powder is made from plant protein in its main products: soy in Life Shake Soy and Energizing Soy Protein, and pea in Life Shake Plant. The only animal-based option in the current US range is the Performance Advanced Physique whey, which is aimed at gym-goers rather than the meal-shake buyer. That makes Shaklee mostly a plant-protein brand, which is why this review sits in our <a href="/best-plant-based-protein-powder/">best plant-based protein powder</a> cluster.
          </p>

          <p>
            Life Shake Soy uses what Shaklee calls a proprietary protein blend: soy protein concentrate, soy protein isolate, added L-leucine, organic chia seed protein and organic pumpkin seed protein. Shaklee says the soy is non-GMO and sourced in North America. Life Shake Plant uses the same structure with pea protein in place of the two soy ingredients. Both add a fiber blend, a prebiotic blend of organic ancient grains (amaranth, buckwheat, millet, quinoa and chia), dry MCT oil, flaxseed and papain and bromelain enzymes.
          </p>

          <p>
            Energizing Soy Protein is the older, simpler product, and it is still on Shaklee's US site. Per its supplement facts at the time of writing, three tablespoons (28 g) of the vanilla version give 14 g of protein and 110 calories. The ingredient list is short: soy protein isolate, fructose, dextrose, soy lecithin, natural vanilla flavor and guar gum. That means 9 g of added sugar per serving, which is the main thing that separates it from the newer zero-sugar Life Shake.
          </p>

          <p>
            So when someone asks what a Shaklee protein drink is, the honest answer is a soy or pea meal shake with leucine added. It is not a pure protein isolate like the ones in our <a href="/best-soy-protein-powder/">best soy protein powder</a> guide. About a quarter of each Life Shake serving by weight is non-protein: fiber, oils, flavors and the vitamin premix. That is good for a meal replacement and less good if you only wanted protein.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
